    {
      "id": "tiktok-7709939284836502806",
      "number": 5,
      "title": "You didn't ignore the deadline. You couldn't see it. CAPTION You didn't ignore the deadline. You couldn't see it. You had the same two weeks as everyone else. You just found out it was due the moment it turned into tomorrow. ADHD brains often sort time into two boxes: now and not now. Anything in \"not now\" feels like it doesn't exist yet. It's called time blindness, and it's why the panic always arrives on the last day. So drag the deadline into \"now\". Put the due date somewhere you look every day, like your lock screen, and give today one small piece of it. Ten minutes counts. Same deadline. Seen sooner.",
      "caption": "You didn't ignore the deadline. You couldn't see it. CAPTION You didn't ignore the deadline. You couldn't see it. You had the same two weeks as everyone else. You just found out it was due the moment it turned into tomorrow. ADHD brains often sort time into two boxes: now and not now. Anything in \"not now\" feels like it doesn't exist yet. It's called time blindness, and it's why the panic always arrives on the last day. So drag the deadline into \"now\". Put the due date somewhere you look every day, like your lock screen, and give today one small piece of it. Ten minutes counts. Same deadline. Seen sooner.",
